From: ginux-watch-agent <actions@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 20:09:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tests(instance): pin id and hostname identifier validation
 edges

### What
Pins `validate` identifier rules for both id and hostname: empty/spaced rejected, dotted alnum accepted, hostname checked independently.

### Why it matters
Hostname defaults to id, so suites that never set a distinct hostname cannot detect a skipped hostname check. Removing either validation call survives today.

### Mutation evidence (fail-then-pass)
| Mutant | Existing suite | New test |
|---|---|---|
| skip `validate_identifier(self.id...)` | PASS (survives) | FAIL (killed) |
| skip `validate_identifier(self.hostname...)` | PASS (survives) | FAIL (killed) |

Baseline: PASS. Reproduce: `cargo test -p ginux-instance --lib validate_pins_identifier`.

Prepared with AI assistance; reviewed by me.
---
 crates/ginux-instance/src/lib.rs | 25 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 25 insertions(+)

diff --git a/crates/ginux-instance/src/lib.rs b/crates/ginux-instance/src/lib.rs
index d5f17444..76cc98be 100644
--- a/crates/ginux-instance/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/ginux-instance/src/lib.rs
@@ -3120,4 +3120,29 @@ failure = "stop"
         c.memory_mib = 15;
         assert!(c.validate().is_err());
     }
+
+    #[test]
+    fn validate_pins_identifier_and_hostname_edges() {
+        let src = VALID.replace(
+            "[resources]",
+            "[identity]\nhostname = \"host.example\"\n\n[resources]",
+        );
+        let mut c = InstanceConfig::parse(src.as_bytes()).unwrap();
+        assert_eq!(c.hostname.as_bytes(), b"host.example");
+        assert!(c.validate().is_ok());
+        // id edges: empty and space rejected, alnum accepted
+        c.id = Text::from_bytes(b"").unwrap();
+        assert!(c.validate().is_err());
+        c.id = Text::from_bytes(b"bad id").unwrap();
+        assert!(c.validate().is_err());
+        c.id = Text::from_bytes(b"demo").unwrap();
+        assert!(c.validate().is_ok());
+        // hostname edges are validated independently of id
+        c.hostname = Text::from_bytes(b"bad host").unwrap();
+        assert!(c.validate().is_err());
+        c.hostname = Text::from_bytes(b"").unwrap();
+        assert!(c.validate().is_err());
+        c.hostname = Text::from_bytes(b"host-2.example").unwrap();
+        assert!(c.validate().is_ok());
+    }
 }
